With this study in cognitive neuroscience we seek to find out how humans represent knowledge about relationships between objects. The study takes place on two consecutive days. On day 1, you are asked to track a bee that is flying between flowers shown on the monitor and you are asked some questions about what you have seen (ca. 45 min). On day 2, you are asked some additional questions about what you have seen the day before (ca. 20 min). The payment is contingent on completing both parts of the study, which takes 1:05 hour in total. This is part 1 of the study. Note that you can only access the second part 16 hours after completing this study and after we have sent you an invitation. We further like to ask you to complete the second part relatively fast, i.e. approximately within 32 hours after the start of the first part, or approximately 16 hours after the invitation to the second part.

